# TG-04 stage B, the architect's path as typed by hand (make walk-tg-login): the desktop of
# make run-tg-login (interactive, QEMU's cocoa display without zoom-to-fit, scale 1) on a
# copy of the kept volume, with no network (the volume may hold the architect's api id and
# hash: nothing reaches Telegram, tgd starts with --no-probe). The first terminal is closed
# and comes back with a desktop to give windows (overlay 0004); in it tgd --window & and
# tg &; the window shows the login's phone form (Next in accent, 3b4f6b).
serial init: gui: gpu on its own page
serial compd: 1024x768
screen Type help to begin, or help tour.
screen ~> _
# Closed (its frame's close button) and opened again by init, with the panel.
click 89 87
serial init: the terminal was closed
pause 4000
window
screen ~> _
type tgd --window --no-probe &\r
prefix tgd: the window's socket is /home/.config/tgd/window.sock
prefix tgd: login: starting
type tg &\r
pause 8000
click 500 119
pause 1500
region 349 412 5 12 3b4f6b
shot tgl-phone
# The dock's terminal tile (x 327: the dock has the room chip and + now) opens another
# terminal, from the panel, which can give windows too.
click 327 722
pause 3000
shot tgl-term
